commit message:
Pecan dataset import mostly complete- both 1 minute and 15 minute data;
Rest depends on standardized appliance naming;
Also need to see what to do for grid and solar

 added SVO, SV & SVP rule from ruiting;
changed the name of those-rule to det-rule;
modified det-rule so as to handle that, this, these determiners.

Reverted some changes that appeared in merge conflicts

Removed check from agent as it is already performed in demo;
check is still available in attention_allocation_agent

// XXX It is common for cogserver code to upcast, without any
// runtime checking, (i.e. without using dynamic_cast) to class
// RequestClassInfo, and then dereference the "help" string.
// This occurs, for example, when the user types "help asdf" at
// the command shell, and the "asdf" command does not exist.
// The unchecked cast and access causes a crash. The correct fix
// would be to not cast all over the place. But that's a lot of
// work, since & not * is used all over the place. So, for now,
// this fix will do the trick.  XXX

modified:
  opencog/server/Registry.h

fixed compile error in UseCountUTest.cxxtest :
    error: no matching function for call to ‘min(size_t&, long unsigned int)’
    isz = std::min(isz, 2010UL);

fixed compile error in UseCountUTest.cxxtest :
    error: no matching function for call to ‘min(size_t&, long unsigned int)’
    isz = std::min(isz, 2010UL);

misc documentation cleanup/clarification;
log the scheme evaluation at debug level not info level.
some scaffloding for yet another evaluator.

Move metapopulation code under moses/metapopulation

Split metapopulation.{h,cc} into metapopulation.{h,cc},
metapop_params.{h,cc} and deme_expander.{h,cc}

Add a new test for matching links.
At the moment, this test will fail; 
I need to fix pattern matcher first to get it to work right.

cleanup the processing of the tail-end of the document;
delete the disconnected senses, so that they don't interfere
with scoring.

wrap long lines to fit into an 80-column terminal;
add instructions on how to build an optimized 
binary.

Fix cogserver crash on boost:asio race condition

cogserver is crashing because boost:asio was prematurely calling
destructors on classes that were still in use.  This was effing
painful to debug.

    // Some details: basically, the remote end of the socket "fires and
    // forgets" a bunch of commands, and then closes the socket before
    // these requests have completed.  boost:asio notices that the
    // remote socket has closed, and so decides its a good day to call
    // destructors. But of course, its not ...

Add convenience wrapppers for adding linkts to the atom space;
Simplify the pattern test case to use the convenience wrappers;
this makes the test case more legible.

atomspace: rip out the TLB

This boils the ocean. Probably a bunch of unit tests fail after this;
they will have to be repaired by hand, one by one :-(

Attempted partial fix for missing boost math library;
according to the cmake documentation, this should work,
but in fact, my cmake utterly fails for this task :-(

Set all methods of bscore_base virtual

bscore_base::min_improv() and bscore_base::set_complexity_coef() need
to be virtual, otherwise if an inherited instance is referenced by a
pointer of type bscore_base the non-virtual methods of that base are
called instead of the inherited instance.

Frankly it still astonishes me that after 10 years of C++ experimence
I can still be confused... But the following experiment set it
clearly, look at this code

#include <iostream>

struct A {
    void truc() const { std::cout << "A" << std::endl; }
};

struct B : public A {
    void truc() const { std::cout << "B" << std::endl; }
};

int main() {
    B b;
    const A& a(b);

    a.truc();
    b.truc();
}

It outputs

A
B

So const A& a(b) has changed the method B::truc to A::truc.

But if I put virtual in front of the declaration of A::truc then it
works, the output is

B
B

Fix extra ';'

test/openglshaderuniforms.cpp:26:2: warning: extra ';' [-Wpedantic]

 };

  ^

